---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Kilnbook for schools"
	description="Wheel booking, kiln firing queues and class rosters for school and college ceramics departments, built around a semester timetable."
>
	<section class="band-dark page-hero">
		<div class="wrap">
			<p class="eyebrow">For schools</p>
			<h1>A ceramics room that runs on the timetable.</h1>
			<p class="lede narrow">
				One or two kilns, a semester of classes and a room full of students who want a wheel in the
				twenty minutes between lectures. Kilnbook keeps the wheels, the firings and the rosters in one
				place, so the department technician is not the booking system.
			</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Wheel time between classes</h2>
		<p>
			Students reserve a wheel or a hand-building table from their phone in one-hour blocks, so a free
			period between classes turns into real time on the wheel. You decide how many hours a week each
			student gets and how far ahead they can book, and freed-up slots appear on the calendar as soon
			as someone cancels.
			<a href="/features/wheel-time">How wheel booking works</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Firings without the shelf of mystery pots</h2>
		<p>
			Students log each piece when it goes on the bisque shelf, and it joins the right load for the
			right kiln. You can see how full each load is, keep a firing log for every kiln, and text
			students when their work is ready to collect, before the end of term rather than after it.
			<a href="/features/firings">How firing queues work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Classes set up once a semester</h2>
		<p>
			Set up each course as a fixed series for the semester, like Ceramics 1 on Mondays and Wednesdays.
			Instructors see their roster, mark attendance from the studio tablet and leave notes for whoever
			teaches the next session. Evening drop-ins for staff or the community can sit alongside them.
			<a href="/features/classes">How classes work</a>.
		</p>

		<h2>Which plan?</h2>
		<p>
			Most departments with one or two kilns fit the Studio plan, which covers up to 3 kilns with
			unlimited members, so every enrolled student can have an account.
			<a href="/pricing">Compare plans</a>.
		</p>
	</section>

	<section class="wrap section narrow">
		<h2>Questions departments ask</h2>
		<div class="faq">
			<details>
				<summary>Is there pricing for schools?</summary>
				<p>
					Yes. School ceramics programs and registered nonprofits get 30% off any plan. Mention it
					when you book a demo.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>How do we add a new class of students each semester?</summary>
				<p>
					Upload a CSV of names and emails from your class list, and we map the columns for you during
					setup.
				</p>
			</details>
			<details>
				<summary>What if the department adds a fourth kiln?</summary>
				<p>
					The Studio plan covers up to 3 kilns. You can move to Collective, which has no kiln limit,
					at any point in the month, and we prorate the difference on your next invoice.
				</p>
			</details>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="cta-band">
		<div class="wrap">
			<h2>Get your ceramics room off the sign-up sheet.</h2>
			<p>We will walk through a week of your timetable and show you how it looks in Kilnbook.</p>
			<a href="/contact" class="btn btn-dark">Book a demo</a>
		</div>
	</section>
</Base>
